{title: The Bride Song}
{artist: Amy Denson}
{key: A}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 90}

{c: Verse 1}
[A] We received a [D5/A] wedding [F] invitation to our [A] hearts

[A] A wedding we’d not [D5/A] heard of, but of [F] which we’d be a [A] part

[F] The Lord called us all by [G] name
[F] to be a woman standing without [G] shame

The Father draws [A] near

{c: Verse 2}
[A] Our lamps are burning [D5/A] brightly and we’re [F] waiting for Your [A] call

[A] The wedding feast is [D5/A] reserved for those who have [F] given You their [A] all

[F] Lord, the time is drawing [G] near
[F] We bow down with holy [G] fear

Father, call us [A] home

{c: Chorus}

[A] Lord, we’re Your [G] bride 
[G] We give our lives to You, a pure and holy [A] sacrifice
[A] Lord, You’re our [G] prize
[G] We want to be presented blameless in Your [A] sight 

[A] Lord, we’re Your [G] bride 
[G] We give our lives to You, a pure and holy [A] sacrifice
[A] Lord, You’re our [G] prize
[G] We want to be presented blameless in Your [A] sight 

